      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "The quote process was fairly straight forward and easy to follow. There were a few hiccups for the installation, due to weather and then the installer not arriving for the booked time slot. No communication for that, I had to follow up. That really wasted my time.There were issues with the installation where my instructions were obviously not passed on to the installer and even though the installer contacted me twice on the day I was never asked for my preference for installing the inverter in my desired location, next the the meter box and not over the top which is crazy. I was there on site in the morning but as mentioned the installer did not turn up.I have been building off grid dollar systems for write a number of years so am not ignorant about installations etc .Then the fun started. They expected full payment minus $500 for peace of mind till a solution was found for the issue with a wrongly placed inverter. They did number something about safety and the inverter but that's not their call or prerogative to decide without consultation.It's been weeks now and still no solution. I have not paid the remaining amount as the job is not completed. The lady on the phone also needs to brush up on customer skills. I'm not impressed.This could be a one off but they may have in house communication issues which will happen again. Uni industries did not meet expectations. I'm still waiting.... I may file a complaint with fair trading if the issue isn't rectified within the next week. They have had plenty of time. I run my own business and will jump to fix any problems ASAP.",
